## 12. Suggested Reading Order For Another AI

If you only have 5 minutes:
1. Read [wiki.repo](/home/ethan/work/projects/running-ai-coach/wiki.repo)
2. Read [AGENTS.md](/home/ethan/work/projects/running-ai-coach/AGENTS.md)
3. Read [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](/home/ethan/work/projects/running-ai-coach/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md)
4. Read [api/app/api/routes/chat.py](/home/ethan/work/projects/running-ai-coach/api/app/api/routes/chat.py)
5. Read [api/app/services/chat_orchestrator.py](/home/ethan/work/projects/running-ai-coach/api/app/services/chat_orchestrator.py)
6. Read [api/app/services/analysis_engine.py](/home/ethan/work/projects/running-ai-coach/api/app/services/analysis_engine.py)

If you are changing product behaviour:
1. confirm whether the change belongs in `chat_orchestrator`, `analysis_engine`, `report_builder`, or `coach_commentary`
2. keep rule-layer facts deterministic
3. do not move numeric truth into the LLM
4. check whether the change affects COROS flow, FIT flow, or both

## 13. Practical Dev Notes

Typical commands:

Backend:
```bash
cd api
python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e .
uvicorn app.main:app --reload --port 8010
```

Frontend:
```bash
cd web
npm install
npm run dev
```

Useful validation:
```bash
cd web && npm run lint
cd api && .venv/bin/python -c "from app.api.router import api_router; print('ok')"
```

## 14. What To Trust Most

When docs disagree, trust in this order:
1. route files in `api/app/api/routes/`
2. service implementations in `api/app/services/`
3. frontend page in `web/src/app/page.tsx`
4. [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](/home/ethan/work/projects/running-ai-coach/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md)
5. [README.md](/home/ethan/work/projects/running-ai-coach/README.md)

That order matters because the repo has evolved from an upload-first MVP into a COROS chat-first product, and some higher-level docs may lag the code.